{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8af61b6420e4992e34d38e9128ab15f114282c2d8975f421ec4c24d45661e143","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review gate","key_entities":["criteria_routing.json","registry.py","workflow_ops.py","orchestrator.py","plan_review_necessity.md","plan-review.yaml","BUG_TIER_CRITERIA","necessity","CANONICAL_LLM","DET floor","ticket_type=bug"],"problem_keywords":["over-action detection","plan-review gate","bug exemption","necessity criterion","advisory-first","lightweight review tier"],"propositions":["The plan-review gate has no criterion to assess whether a proposed change is actually needed, leaving FixedBench's 35-65% over-action gap unclosed.","Bug tickets short-circuit to bare exempt-PASS with zero LLM calls and no substantive review, preventing any meaningful evaluation of bug fixes.","A new pass-1 advisory criterion 'necessity' must flag plans that add mechanisms without establishing need, accepting well-motivated outcomes and justified no-ops.","Bug tickets must receive a lightweight advisory review tier (DET floor + necessity probe only) instead of exemption, never blocking a bug.","The necessity probe and bug tier must ship as advisory, registered non-orphan, and auto-monitored via the standing effectiveness recorder before promotion to blocking."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787318816061179001,"uuid":"0df609ee-0a74-4d77-8172-930268983b5c"}